@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
title Epic 1 — Building the spatial memory

rectangle "Memory building" {
  card US1_1 [
    **US-1.1  Basir remembers without being asked**
    As a //user//, I want Basir to keep remembering what the camera sees while I walk around,
    so that it can find things I never told it to look for.
    ----
    * The phone streams continuously; ingest never blocks and drops frames under load.
    * Keyframes are kept (1–3 per second, or when the view or pose changes enough), not every frame.
    * Memory covers minutes to hours, not only the last few seconds.
  ]
  card US1_2 [
    **US-1.2  Objects, not just frames**
    As a //user//, I want small objects (keys, remote, mug) remembered on their own,
    so that they are found even when they fill a tiny part of the picture.
    ----
    * Each keyframe is run through an open-vocabulary detector with ~200 household nouns.
    * Every detection gets a SAM mask and a SigLIP embedding of its crop (an Observation).
  ]
  card US1_3 [
    **US-1.3  Each object has a place in the room**
    As a //user//, I want every remembered object to have a 3D position,
    so that Basir can tell me where it is from where I stand now.
    ----
    * Position = median masked depth back-projected with the frame's camera pose.
    * Pose and depth come from ARCore on the phone (or dataset ground truth in development).
  ]
  card US1_4 [
    **US-1.4  One object, one memory entry**
    As a //user//, I want the same bottle seen 50 times to be one object,
    so that answers are not cluttered with duplicates.
    ----
    * A new observation joins a track if embedding similarity > τ_sim and distance < τ_dist (≈0.5 m).
    * A track keeps first_seen, last_seen, a running position and its clearest crop.
  ]
}
US1_1 -[hidden]down- US1_2
US1_2 -[hidden]down- US1_3
US1_3 -[hidden]down- US1_4
@enduml
